// Original Red Alert audio (WP11.7, B11): which of the player's own Red
// Alert sounds replaces which Staalfront sound event. Names only: no audio
// from Red Alert is ever in this repository.
//
// Used only when "Use original Red Alert audio" is on (assets/config/audio.ron
// or `sf_game --ra-audio <path>`). An event whose file is not found keeps
// its CC0 sound from bank.ron (or stays silent if it has none yet).
//
//   sounds: event -> file name inside the MIX archives ("NAME.AUD", or "NAME.V01" for a voice line), or the
//           raw id "#1A2B3C4D" the F1 sound browser shows for entries whose
//           name it does not know.
//   names:  extra file names the sound browser should show instead of ids.
//
// Voice lines (select, move, attack) never exist as a bare ".AUD" in Red
// Alert: they carry a variant as extension. ".Vnn" is the Allied accent and
// ".Rnn" the Soviet accent; infantry lines use the odd variants (01, 03),
// vehicle lines the even ones (00, 02). The loader looks a name up as
// written, so the extension is part of the name. V01 is a default: pick the
// variant by ear in the F1 sound browser (Sound browser > play) and change it
// here.
(
    sounds: {
        "ui.click": "RAMENU1.AUD",
        "unit.select": "AWAIT1.V01",
        "unit.move": "ACKNO.V01",
        "unit.attack": "AFFIRM1.V01",
        "building.placed": "PLACBLDG.AUD",
        "explosion.small": "KABOOM1.AUD",
    },
    names: [
        "MAIN.MIX",
        "REDALERT.MIX",
        "SOUNDS.MIX",
        "SPEECH.MIX",
        "ALLIES.MIX",
        "RUSSIAN.MIX",
        "LOCAL.MIX",
        "CONQUER.MIX",
        "SCORES.MIX",
    ],
)
